      {
        "parameters": {
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "http://ollama:11434/api/chat",
          "sendBody": true,
          "specifyBody": "json",
          "jsonBody": "={{ {\n  model: 'llama3.1:8b-instruct-q4_K_M',\n  messages: [\n    {\n      role: 'system',\n      content: 'You are a classifier for an Architecture pipeline. Analyze the user input and determine the mode, intent, and extract project information.\\n\\nMODE RULES:\\n- mode=chat: For queries, help requests, status checks. Keywords: help, status, list, artifacts, jobs, what, how, show, get, query, ?\\n- mode=execute: For creating/building/generating architecture. Keywords: build, create, generate, make, develop, design a, implement\\n\\nIf input is a single word like \"help\", \"list\", \"jobs\", \"status\" - it is ALWAYS mode=chat.\\nIf input asks a question or requests information - it is mode=chat.\\nOnly use mode=execute when user explicitly wants to CREATE or BUILD something new.\\n\\nPROJECT EXTRACTION (CRITICAL):\\n- ALWAYS extract the projectSlug from the input text\\n- Look for patterns like \"project X\", \"for X\", \"X project\", or project names in the text\\n- The projectSlug should be a lowercase-hyphenated string (e.g., \"healthcare-appointment-scheduler\")\\n- If no project name is found, set projectSlug to null\\n\\nChat intents: help, status, artifacts, jobs, list\\nExecute intents: create, build, generate\\n\\nOutput JSON only.'    },\n    { role: 'user', content: $json.rawInput || $json.requirements }\n  ],\n  stream: false,\n  format: {\n    type: 'object',\n    required: ['mode', 'intent', 'projectSlug'],\n    properties: {\n      mode: { type: 'string', enum: ['chat', 'execute'] },\n      intent: { type: 'string' },\n      projectSlug: { type: 'string', description: 'The project name/slug extracted from the input text, lowercase with hyphens' },\n      requirements: { type: 'string' }\n    }\n  },\n  options: { temperature: 0.1 }\n} }}",
          "options": {}
        },
        "id": "classify-mode",
        "name": "Classify Mode",
